<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huo Qubing</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">140–117 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huo Qubing was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> general of the second century BCE, renowned for his cavalry campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a>. His deep raids into the steppe inflicted major defeats and helped secure the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor">Hexi Corridor</a>. He died young but is remembered as one of the most brilliant commanders against the Xiongnu Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huo-qubing.jpg" alt="Huo Qubing" width="295" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ma Tai (馬駘; C.E.1885-1937) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B8%A1%E6%B2%B3%E5%8F%97%E6%AC%BE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
